{"task":"transcribe","language":"English","duration":82.84737536,"text":" Afro Farms, a farming operation in Kenya, gets a daily update from the farm's own MCP operating system, so its command deck always matches the operation's data underneath. Bills and subscriptions span six entities, 71 recurring bills in one register. Every two weeks, an automation searches five mailboxes for invoices, renewals, payment confirmations, and cancellations, and updates the register in place. It marks bills paid or canceled, adds new ones, keeps the deadlines current, and stores evidence for every change. The rule is simple. Nothing is estimated. If an amount can't be verified, it's marked unverified. The CEO dashboard turns it into four screens. The brief, decisions, dates, and every bill. And a separate task emails only the urgent items. I also audited every subscription plan and tool. Oversized storage plans came down. Unused AI and software seats were canceled. Plans like Matan, Versal, and Wadi were downgraded. Afrofarm's recurring costs dropped from about €1,380 a month to about €420. Altogether, that's around $33,000 a year already saved, and about €35,700 once the last pending cancellation goes through.","words":[{"word":"Afro","start":0.24,"end":0.74},{"word":"Farms,","start":0.74,"end":1.1},{"word":"a","start":1.1,"end":1.48},{"word":"farming","start":1.48,"end":1.84},{"word":"operation","start":1.84,"end":2.34},{"word":"in","start":2.34,"end":2.54},{"word":"Kenya,","start":2.54,"end":3.6},{"word":"gets","start":3.6,"end":3.66},{"word":"a","start":3.66,"end":3.8},{"word":"daily","start":3.8,"end":4.12},{"word":"update","start":4.12,"end":4.5},{"word":"from","start":4.5,"end":4.72},{"word":"the","start":4.72,"end":4.88},{"word":"farm's","start":4.88,"end":5.24},{"word":"own","start":5.24,"end":5.6},{"word":"MCP","start":5.6,"end":6.38},{"word":"operating","start":6.38,"end":6.9},{"word":"system,","start":6.9,"end":7.94},{"word":"so","start":7.94,"end":8},{"word":"its","star